            <ArticleTitle>First reported use of drug-coated balloon for bioresorbable in-scaffold restenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>676-678</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.26803</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is the first documented case of a drug-coated balloon strategy for the treatment of bioresorbable in-scaffold restenosis caused by diffuse neointimal proliferation. This case can provide an alternative treatment option in this setting, avoiding potential problems related to further bulky metallic stents in a patient where a different strategy was initially planned. © 2016 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2016 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
